-- title:
--   Fixing every coset-graph vertex forces a rational scalar
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $R$ a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ with the additive relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q'$ and $r\nmid N$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$. Write $\mathrm{Loc}=\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ and $\mathrm{Vert}=\mathrm{Loc}^\times/(\text{level } R\,v)$, where the level subgroup is generated by the units of the local box of $R$ at $v$ together with the scalar units at $v$. If $\gamma\in\mathbb{H}^\times$ has the property that, for every $g\in\mathrm{Loc}^\times$, the classes of `toLoc v γ * g` and of $g$ in $\mathrm{Vert}$ coincide, then $\gamma=c\cdot 1$ for some $c\in\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   This is the faithfulness statement for the action of $\mathbb{H}^\times$ by left translation on the vertex set of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_r)$ at a place $v$ where the quaternion algebra and the Eichler order are both split: the kernel of the action consists of rational scalars. It is used in the analysis of the coset graph, for the construction of a normal subgroup of finite index with no nontrivial torsion and for the computation of dart stabilisers.
